# Grants the interactively logged-in user (via systemd-logind's seat
# ACLs, TAG+="uaccess" -- no group to manage, no relogin needed beyond
# the session already active) read/write access to every hidraw
# device, needed for VIA (usevia.app) to configure a VIA-compatible
# keyboard without running as root.
#
# Broader than "just VIA keyboards" is unavoidable here, not a
# shortcut: there is no vendor/product ID or other kernel-visible
# marker that identifies a device as VIA-compatible, so VIA's own
# Linux setup instructions ask for exactly this same all-hidraw access
# (see e.g. https://github.com/the-via/app/issues/292, where this
# breadth is the documented, accepted tradeoff, not a bug). This is why
# the package shipping this rule is opt-in (System Tuning profile),
# never installed by default.
ACTION!="remove", KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"
